fallback span `<<>>` once, around the middle of the budget (after some
unconstrained reasoning but while plenty of budget remains). This preserves
the required `<< >>` syntax while leaving many later steps available for
the model to finish the actual answer.
4. After the fallback has been inserted, immediately return to unconstrained
decoding; we never try to synthesize arithmetic content inside the span.
This avoids the malformed-constrained-content failures entirely.
5. If the budget is so small that a mid-budget insertion is impossible, fall
back to a last-moment insertion only when exactly two steps remain.
6. EOS remains terminal.
