//    steps for a minimal fallback span `<<>>`: when exactly two steps remain,
//    call `OpenConstrainedSpan`; on the next iteration the empty constrained
//    prefix is complete, so immediately call `CloseConstrainedSpan`.
// 4. To avoid the previous "EOS before fallback" problem, we also cap the
//    unconstrained tail: if only two steps remain, we stop free-form decoding
//    and spend them on the fallback. This preserves the delimiter guarantee
//    whenever generation has not already terminated on EOS.
// 5. EOS is terminal.
