So this revision uses a simple three-phase policy:
- If we inherit an active constrained span, finish it conservatively:
close immediately when complete; otherwise allow only a tiny bounded number
of constrained steps, then abandon safely.
- If we are outside constrained mode and still have not guaranteed any span,
force exactly one minimal closed span `<<>>` very early (on the first loop
iteration when starting outside). This guarantees the required delimiters
before any possible EOS, and because the span is empty it avoids malformed
arithmetic-content failures.
