the amount of free-form continuation so the model is less likely to wander
into long repetitive explanations. EOS remains terminal.
Relative to the previous attempt, the key changes are:
(a) move the guaranteed `<<>>` insertion from the final two steps to the
beginning of outside-mode generation, eliminating the "EOS before
fallback" failure;
(b) keep the forced span minimal and immediately closed, avoiding malformed
constrained syntax;
(c) bound the post-span unconstrained tail to reduce unfinished rambling and
improve the chance that the answer stays concise.

