Minimal fix: keep the strategy shape exactly the same, but strengthen the
break guards so they only fire when some progress has already happened
(`steps > 0`). If no progress has happened yet, the existing logic falls
through to either open the fallback constrained span or take an unconstrained
step, which makes the postcondition provable without changing the overall
policy.

