  Rationale: Step-by-step math-solution CSD with delimiter-aware modes plus lightweight
arithmetic-context steering. The strategy tracks whether generation is
currently inside a constrained `<< ... >>` span and, when inside, the exact
constrained-prefix contents `currentConstrainedOut`. It also derives a small
local context signal from the active span: whether the span already contains
arithmetic-looking tokens such as "+", "-", "*", "/", or "=".
Outside constrained spans, generation is free-form so the model can write
natural language reasoning. When a token containing "<<" appears, the
strategy enters constrained mode with an empty constrained prefix. Inside a
span, if the parser says the prefix is complete, the strategy closes the span
immediately with `>>`. Otherwise it chooses the next constrained token using
an adaptive policy: if the grammar is narrow, use AdaptiveConstrainedStep
with caller-supplied token groups; if the span already looks arithmetic,
additionally boost those groups manually before constrained sampling. This
keeps arithmetic computations well-formed while still allowing natural model
preferences within the parser's valid-next set.

